<p>Curtain’s Up Drama School was established in 2011 by Sarah-Jayne Quigley</p>
<p>Curtain’s Up is a dedicated Speech &amp; Drama School in Knocklyon, Firhouse &amp; Tallaght, Dublin.</p>
<p>My aim is to provide small class sizes and individual attention to allow children and young adults to flourish and promote confidence.</p>
<p>The Speech &amp; Drama class is a place where children and teenagers feel safe and are free to express themselves in a structured environment. Imagination and creativity are praised and encouraged. I set high standards for my pupils and I always spur them to go that little bit further and work that little bit harder. The drama class allows the freedom to learn, experiment and play.</p>
<p>The Speech &amp; Drama class should be a place where everybody is equal and each child and young adult can express themselves without fear.</p>
<p>Drama classes in both terms include;</p>
<ul>
  <li>Poetry</li>
  <li>Scripted Performance</li>
  <li>Improvisation</li>
  <li>Character Creation</li>
  <li>Mime</li>
  <li>Communication</li>
  <li>Games</li>
  <li>Creative Drama</li>
  <li>Vocal Training</li>
  <li>Confidence Building</li>
  <li>Audition Preparation</li>
  <li>Acting for Camera</li>
</ul>
<p>Term One includes preparation for the Irish Board of Speech &amp; Drama exams. I’m delighted to say that last year, all students that took part in the exams did extremely well!</p>
<p>Term Three includes a relaxed performance for family and friends.</p>
<p>See you in September!</p>
